# Docs

- `README.md` is the Cloudera blueprint landing page. Keep Overview, Demo, Use Case, Key Features, Quickstart, Software Components, Target Audience, Repository Structure, Prerequisites, Hardware Requirements, and Documentation.
- Catalog fields live in `METADATA.yaml`. Do not drop identity, classification, tags, product_mapping, publisher, source, or date keys.
- Keep architecture, identity, CLI, Spark, Hive, AMP, phases, inventory, and tests as separate files under `docs/`.
- Inventory and test result tables must never contain tokens, passcodes, or private keys.
- When adding a phase, hop, or CLI command, update `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/phases.md`, and `docs/operator-cli.md` in the same change.
- Spark allowlist, Livy, WebHDFS, or MCP Spark tools: update `docs/spark.md`. Hive MCP (`/mcp/hive`), JDBC inventory, or `/cdp/hive` 404: update `docs/hive.md`. Impala MCP (`/mcp/impala`), CDW JDBC, or `/cdp/impala` 404: update `docs/impala.md`. Do not publish `/cdp/hive` or `/cdp/impala`.
- New gateway behavior needs a test ID in `docs/testing.md` before it is "done".
- Prefer links to APISIX Learning Center and Cloudera Knox docs over copying vendor pages verbatim.
